  "summary": "This paper reports stamped, coplanar solid-state all-MXene micro-supercapacitors prepared from LiF/HCl MILD-derived Ti3C2Tx or Ti3CNTx inks. Six distinct electrochemically identified device variants are extractable from the supplied paper: standard interdigitated, yin yang, and spiral Ti3C2Tx; yin yang Ti3CNTx; a thin interdigitated Ti3C2Tx device made using tenfold-diluted ink; and a cylindrical-stamp rolled interdigitated Ti3C2Tx device. The headline I-Ti3C2Tx device gave the best reported capacitance, 61 mF cm\u22122 at 25 \u00b5A cm\u22122. Mass loading, BET surface area, pore metrics, d-spacing, tortuosity, gravimetric capacitance, and device volumetric capacitance were not reported."
